{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/src/backend/vespa_app.py::VespaQueryClient.get_sim_maps_from_query", "what_it_does": "Runs the _sim ranking query through asyncio.run and returns the summaryfeatures value of each hit, raising ValueError if a hit lacks it.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [260, 286], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Not writable inside this unit: the method receives only query, q_embs, ranking and idx_to_token and must issue its own Vespa query. The duplicate comes from main.py, where fetch_results (lines 215-220) and get_and_store_sim_maps (line 263, ranking_sim) both query Vespa with the same q_embs. Removing it needs the first response passed in from main.py, a caller change beyond this unit that is not part of the edit."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/src/backend/vespa_app.py::VespaQueryClient.results_to_search_results", "what_it_does": "Adds a None-valued sim_map_ placeholder field to every hit's fields dict for each non-filtered token and returns the children list.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [319, 331], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Not writable inside this unit: deciding that a sim map file already exists needs query_id and SIM_MAP_DIR (main.py lines 122 and 304-311), which this method does not receive. The None value is the only signal the app.py branch (lines 561-580) uses to choose SimMapButtonPoll, so changing it means changing state outside the unit."}, {"label": "b", "lines": [325, 327], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "The should_filter_token call is inside the list comprehension at lines 323-327, which runs once per call over idx_to_token before the for loop at line 328. It is not run per hit, so the claimed per-token-per-hit cost does not occur. The nested loop at lines 328-330 only assigns dict keys."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/src/backend/vespa_app.py::VespaQueryClient.format_q_embs", "what_it_does": "Converts a query-embedding tensor into a dict that maps each row index to that row as a Python float list.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [204, 214], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "The per-row work in this unit is the comprehension at line 214 (emb.tolist() for each row via enumerate). The numpy binarisation the suspicion names is in float_to_binary_embedding and is not part of this edit. Repair: if isinstance(q_embs, torch.Tensor), return dict(enumerate(q_embs.tolist())), and keep the old loop for any other input. Mechanism: one bulk conversion replaces one tensor-row view and one tolist per row, and on an accelerator one host transfer instead of one per row. Output is the same dict with int keys and float-list values, a 0-d tensor still raises TypeError, and non-tensor inputs take the unchanged path. Readers of the dict are query_vespa_bm25 (line 130) and query_vespa_colpali (line 405), both in this file and both only pass it on. The saving is small because the row count is the query token count."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/src/backend/vespa_app.py::VespaQueryClient.float_to_binary_embedding", "what_it_does": "Converts each query-embedding vector in a dict into a sign-bit packed int8 list, keeps at most 64 entries, and logs a warning when the input has 64 or more.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [155, 178], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "The contract check fails for a one-shot numpy version. The unit accepts any dict of lists: an empty dict returns {} today and would need a special case, and ragged rows convert one by one without error, while a stacked array raises ValueError. The only caller (query_vespa_colpali line 406) passes uniform rows, but the contract covers every input, so the stacked form cannot be used unguarded, and a guarded form falls back to the loop. The work is at most 64 rows of 128 floats, so the saving is also small."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/src/backend/vespa_app.py::VespaQueryClient.query_vespa_bm25", "what_it_does": "Sends the query text, an optional qt tensor, and the bm25 or bm25_sim ranking to Vespa, and returns the formatted JSON response.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [129, 153], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "The session is built by app.asyncio(connections=1). In pyvespa, VespaAsync.__aenter__ calls _open_httpr_client, which builds a new httpr.AsyncClient, and __aexit__ closes it (application.py, VespaAsync class near lines 2339-2375), so each call builds and closes its own client. A shared client would need the client= argument (application.py line 370) and an owner that closes it, which is outside this unit. This method is also reached from get_sim_maps_from_query through asyncio.run on a separate event loop (vespa_app.py line 276, bm25_sim path), so a client bound to the server loop is not verified safe there."}, {"label": "b", "lines": [129, 153], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "Repair: build query_embedding with format_q_embs and include 'input.query(qt)' in the body only when sim_map is true. Verified in application/schemas/pdf_page.sd: the bm25 profile (lines 62-95) reads query(qt) only inside function similarities, its first-phase is bm25(title) + bm25(text), and it has no second-phase or summary-features. The only consumer of similarities is bm25_sim's summary-features quantized (lines 96-105), so the non-sim bm25 call never reads qt. Mechanism: each non-sim BM25 query stops converting the full token-by-128 tensor to Python lists, serialising it as JSON, and having Vespa parse it. Sim-map queries still send qt. Sole-caller evidence: query_vespa_bm25 is reached from get_result_from_query (line 250) with sim_map False from main.py fetch_results and with sim_map True from get_sim_maps_from_query; the return value is response.json in both cases. Not verified against a running Vespa: that an unused declared input raises no error when omitted."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/src/backend/vespa_app.py::VespaQueryClient.get_full_image_from_vespa", "what_it_does": "Fetches the base64 full_image field for one document id from Vespa and returns it as a string.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [288, 314], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "pyvespa creates a new httpr.AsyncClient on each context entry and closes it on exit (application.py VespaAsync __aenter__/_open_httpr_client and __aexit__/_close_httpr_client). A reuse repair needs a long-lived client passed through client= (application.py line 370). That cannot be built inside this unit without calling pyvespa's private _open_httpr_client or copying its mTLS and token header setup, and nothing in the unit would close it, so the close belongs in a main.py shutdown hook outside the unit. Sole caller is main.py line 329 in the full_image route. The saved handshake cost was not measured."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/src/backend/vespa_app.py::VespaQueryClient.get_suggestions", "what_it_does": "Runs a regex match over the questions field for a query string and returns the unique questions found, minus the artifact string.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [333, 370], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Same pyvespa lifecycle as the other session items: app.asyncio creates and closes an httpr.AsyncClient per call (application.py VespaAsync __aenter__/__aexit__). Reuse needs a long-lived client with an owner that closes it, which cannot be written inside this unit without pyvespa private methods or a main.py shutdown hook. The sole caller is the /suggestions route (main.py lines 344-350), which fires per typed query, so the per-call cost is high, but the in-unit repair is not available."}, {"label": "b", "lines": [333, 370], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "The repair would change the result set. questions is an attribute-only array<string> (pdf_page.sd lines 50-52, indexing summary and attribute, no index), so matches scans values with a substring regex. A prefix or contains form matches a different set of strings, so the returned list changes. A prefix index needs a schema change and redeploy outside this unit."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/src/frontend/app.py::AboutThisDemo", "what_it_does": "Builds the About This Demo page component, including the embedded Hugging Face dataset viewer iframe.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [438, 443], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "The unit returns the FT component tree that main.py line 158 renders directly. Adding loading='lazy' to the Iframe changes that returned markup, which the contract covers. Visible rendering is also a change, so the edit is outside the contract even though deferring the viewer load is benign."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/src/frontend/app.py::SimMapButtonPoll", "what_it_does": "Builds the disabled spinner button for a pending sim map that re-requests /get_sim_map on a fixed interval.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [495, 504], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "The unit returns the Button markup. Changing the hx_trigger value from every 0.5s to a longer interval changes that returned attribute, which the contract covers. It also changes how long a finished sim map waits before appearing. The docstring at main.py lines 300-302 says 1 second, so code and docstring disagree, but that does not license a change to the returned markup."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/src/frontend/layout.py::Logo", "what_it_does": "Builds the Vespa logo as two img elements, one for light mode and one for dark mode, inside a sized Div.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [104, 117], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "The unit returns the Div with both Img children, used by layout.py line 159, so any single-image repair changes the returned markup, which the contract covers. A picture element with a prefers-color-scheme media query would not match this page: the theme comes from localStorage or the dark class toggled by the theme button (layout.py lines 31-32 and the MutationObserver at lines 96-98), so a CSS media query would show the wrong logo. A class-driven single image would need JavaScript or a different markup, which again changes the output."}]}

