{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/src/backend/colpali.py::SimMapGenerator.gen_similarity_maps", "what_it_does": "Loads each input image as RGB with a copy and its size, computes normalized similarity maps for every query token, and yields each non-filtered token's blended PNG as base64 with its image index, token and token index.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [83, 86], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Only the size is read downstream (_blend_image never touches img), but _load_image wraps decode failures as ValueError via convert('RGB'). A lazy size read with Image.open would accept a truncated or corrupt body and produce maps where today it raises ValueError, and a missing file would need the same wrapping. The exception contract changes, so the repair is rejected."}, {"label": "b", "lines": [83, 88], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Verified dead store: processed_images is appended at lines 83 and 88 and never read. Removing it stops no computation or I/O; the only effect is that each decoded page is released after its copy instead of at function return, a memory-residency change with no work saved, so there is no energy mechanism."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/src/backend/colpali.py::SimMapGenerator._blend_image", "what_it_does": "Resizes a similarity map to a fraction of the page size, colours it with viridis, and returns it as a base64-encoded PNG string; the img argument is not used.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [162, 194], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Confirmed img is never referenced in the body (lines 162-194) and the only caller is gen_similarity_maps at colpali.py:103 (repo grep). Dropping the parameter removes a reference pass that stops no work, so there is no energy mechanism. The base64 round trip (encoded here, decoded at main.py:290) is a separate change that would alter the yielded type from str to bytes across colpali.py:106 and main.py:288-290; it is not folded into this repair and is not decided here."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/src/backend/colpali.py::SimMapGenerator._prepare_similarity_map_tensor", "what_it_does": "Builds a zero float32 tensor of shape (maps, query tokens, n_patch, n_patch) and fills it with each Vespa summary cell's value at its query token and patch position, skipping patches at or beyond the image sequence length.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [126, 160], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "The loop at lines 142-159 performs one torch element assignment per Vespa cell, each with torch dispatch overhead, and the cell count scales with documents times query tokens times patches. Edit: inside the existing loop, store each value in a dict keyed by (idx, query_token, patch // n_patch, patch % n_patch) so later duplicates overwrite earlier ones as today, hoist the image_seq_length lookup out of the loop, then after the loop write all entries with one index_put_ over a float32 value tensor. The mechanism is removing per-cell torch dispatch in favour of one batched kernel; the output tensor, dtype and last-wins values are unchanged. Sole-caller evidence: _prepare_similarity_map_tensor is called only at colpali.py:91; out-of-range rows still raise IndexError, the same exception type."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/src/backend/colpali.py::SimMapGenerator.should_filter_token", "what_it_does": "Returns True when a query token string matches one of a fixed set of filter patterns (special tokens, whitespace, punctuation, leading underscore, the word Question, a lone sentencepiece space).", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [253], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "The premise is only partly right: re.compile on a constant string is served from re's internal cache, so no pattern is recompiled. The removable work is the per-call cache lookup (type and flags check plus dict lookup keyed by the pattern). Edit: move the pattern to a module-level compiled constant and return bool(_TOKEN_FILTER.match(token)). The return value is the same bool for both callers (colpali.py:99 and vespa_app.py:326), and only one new module constant is added. The saving is small, roughly 100 calls per query, but the mechanism is real."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/src/backend/colpali.py::SimMapGenerator.get_query_embeddings_and_token_map", "what_it_does": "Runs the ColPali model on the query and returns its embeddings plus a map from each position to a token string taken by decoding the input ids and re-tokenising the decoded text; the result is cached per query string.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [271, 279], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "convert_ids_to_tokens gives identical strings only if decode followed by tokenize returns the same sequence as the ids, and the code does not establish that. processor.decode is tokenizer.decode with default arguments (colpali_engine interpretability/processor.py:112-113), so spacing cleanup or sentencepiece normalisation could change segmentation for some queries, and the mapping's length could then differ from the q_emb rows. The return value would change for those queries, which the same-return-value rule forbids. The saving is one decode and one tokenize per distinct query (lru_cache at line 258), small beside the model forward at line 273. Side observation, not a verdict: a changed token count would already misalign idx_to_token with the q_emb rows."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/src/main.py::get_and_store_sim_maps", "what_it_does": "In a background thread, runs a second Vespa query for summary features, waits up to 5 seconds for the full images of the result documents, then writes one blended PNG per document and non-filtered token into SIM_MAP_DIR under query_id.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [258, 294], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Every non-filtered token of every result gets a button (frontend/app.py:548-575, results_to_search_results in vespa_app.py:319-331), and each button polls /get_sim_map (app.py:495-500, main.py:297-319) until its PNG exists. The PNGs are needed for this search's UI; deferring or skipping them would leave buttons spinning. A lazy design moves the work to the poll path and changes which files are written at search time, which is outside this unit."}, {"label": "b", "lines": [262, 268], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Verified the ranking is identical: colpali_sim inherits colpali and hybrid_sim inherits hybrid, each overriding only first-phase with the same max_sim_binary expression and adding summary-features quantized (application/schemas/pdf_page.sd lines 241-250 and 386-395). But no edit confined to this unit removes the query: get_fields(sim_map=True) returns only summaryfeatures (vespa_app.py:80-84), so the first query would need changes to its yql and to get_result_from_query, plus fetch_results (main.py:201-239) and this function's signature. Sole-caller evidence: get_and_store_sim_maps is called only at main.py:231 and get_sim_maps_from_query only at main.py:263. The repair reaches fetch_results and the search query the user waits on, so it is rejected here; the saving of one full Vespa retrieval per search is real and is a candidate for a cross-unit change."}, {"label": "c", "lines": [258, 294], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "An early return on existing outputs would skip the Vespa query at line 263, the PNG generation, and the Sim map saved debug records at lines 291-293, which changes the Vespa calls and log records. The check also cannot see index state: query_id is a hash of query and ranking only (main.py:139-141), so after a reindex a repeated query would keep old PNGs where today they are rewritten with current Vespa results. Reuse would only help repeated searches within one process, because the salted hash never repeats across restarts. Rejected on the contract."}, {"label": "d", "lines": [270, 280], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "The time.sleep(0.2) wait at lines 273-277 is off-CPU and bounded by 5 seconds, about 25 wakeups per search at most. The only edit inside the unit is a longer interval, which changes how long after the images arrive the maps start, a timing change the contract does not allow. The event-based alternative needs a signal from the full_image route, which is outside this unit. Rejected: the mechanism is negligible and the timing changes."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/src/main.py::generate_query_id", "what_it_does": "Hashes the query and ranking string into an integer that serves as the query_id shown to the page and used in sim-map file names and log lines.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [139, 141], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Confirmed hash() of bytes is salted per process unless PYTHONHASHSEED is set. But the value is visible: it appears in sim-map button ids and get_sim_map URLs (frontend/app.py:485-500), the ChatResult SSE URL (app.py:751), and sim-map file names (main.py:289, 304). A stable replacement changes every returned id value, and a hex string would also change the return type (callers at main.py:184 and 201). No work stops: nothing reads a cache keyed by query_id before generating (see unit 6 c), so stability saves no energy by itself. Rejected."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/src/main.py::full_image", "what_it_does": "Returns an HTML img element with the full JPEG of a document as a data URI, fetching it from Vespa and writing it to disk on a miss, or reading and base64-encoding the disk copy on a hit.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [322, 341], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "On a disk hit (lines 334-336) every request reopens the JPEG and base64-encodes the whole file. Edit: add a module-level functools.lru_cache(maxsize=N) helper keyed by the file path that returns base64.b64encode(f.read()).decode('utf-8'), call it on the hit branch, and leave the miss branch (lines 328-333) unchanged; the returned Img is identical because the cached string is exactly what the hit branch computes today. The mechanism is skipping the open, read and base64 pass for repeated requests for a document, which the frontend issues on every search (app.py:638, hx_trigger load). Sole-caller evidence: full_image is reached only through the route (app.py:638 hx_get; no other call in the repo), IMG_DIR files are written only at main.py:331, and the readers message_generator (main.py:370) and get_and_store_sim_maps (main.py:269) read the files, not the cache, so they are unaffected. The maxsize bounds the memory cost."}, {"label": "b", "lines": [322, 341], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "The per-result round trip is set by the frontend, which issues one /full_image request per result (app.py:638, hx_trigger load), so batching needs a change outside this unit. Coalescing concurrent misses inside this route would change log records: the waiting request would skip the Full image saved to disk debug line at line 333, and the number of Vespa queries would change. The duplicate-miss case only arises for concurrent requests for the same document. Rejected: the coalescing repair changes log records, and the batching part is outside the unit."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/src/main.py::message_generator", "what_it_does": "Streams Gemini's answer to a query over server-sent events, after waiting up to 10 seconds for the full images of the top documents, with newline characters converted to br tags in the accumulated text.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [364, 382], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Image.open is lazy (header read only), and the wait loop stops as soon as enough images exist, so per tick the reopen work is at most num_images header reads. The obvious repair, keeping opened Image objects across ticks, changes handle lifetime: a file opened while the endpoint is still writing it would be kept and not reopened at the final tick, so the bytes Gemini later reads could differ in that race. That changes what is sent to Gemini, and the saving is a few header reads per 0.2 second tick. Rejected."}, {"label": "b", "lines": [403], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "Line 403 reruns replace over the whole accumulated response_text on every chunk, so the work per chunk grows with the reply. Edit: append only the converted chunk, response_text += chunk.text.replace('\\n', '<br>'), and delete line 403. The output is equal because the pattern is one newline character, so replacing per piece matches replacing the concatenation, and the replacement '<br>' contains no newline so earlier replacements create no new matches; the yields at line 404 carry the same strings. The mechanism is that each chunk no longer rescans and reallocates the full text, so the replace cost per chunk drops from proportional to the whole reply to proportional to the new chunk; the yield still sends the full text, so the saving is a constant factor."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/src/main.py::keepalive", "what_it_does": "Starts a background task at application startup that calls a Vespa keepalive query every 5 seconds and logs each call at debug level.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [133, 136], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "The periodic query is deliberate: vespa_app.py:440-441 documents keepalive as Query Vespa to keep the connection alive, the function is named for it, and main.py:251-255 logs each tick. Changing the interval or stopping it changes the queries issued and the debug records, and removing it would change connection warmth. The only stated purpose in the repo is that docstring, and nothing in the repo says it is unneeded. Rejected as intentional behaviour."}]}

