{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/src/backend/colpali.py::SimMapGenerator.gen_similarity_maps", "what_it_does": "Loads each input image as RGB with a copy and its size, computes normalized similarity maps for every query token, and yields each non-filtered token's blended PNG as base64 with its image index, token and token index.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [83, 86], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Only the size is read downstream (_blend_image never touches img), but _load_image wraps decode failures as ValueError via convert('RGB'). A lazy size read with Image.open would accept a truncated or corrupt body and produce maps where today it raises ValueError, and a missing file would need the same wrapping. The exception contract changes, so the repair is rejected."}, {"label": "b", "lines": [83, 88], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Verified dead store: processed_images is appended at lines 83 and 88 and never read. Removing it stops no computation or I/O; the only effect is that each decoded page is released after its copy instead of at function return, a memory-residency change with no work saved, so there is no energy mechanism."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/src/backend/colpali.py::SimMapGenerator._blend_image", "what_it_does": "Resizes a similarity map to a fraction of the page size, colours it with viridis, and returns it as a base64-encoded PNG string; the img argument is not used.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [162, 194], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Confirmed img is never referenced in the body (lines 162-194) and the only caller is gen_similarity_maps at colpali.py:103 (repo grep). Dropping the parameter removes a reference pass that stops no work, so there is no energy mechanism. The base64 round trip (encoded here, decoded at main.py:290) is a separate change that would alter the yielded type from str to bytes across colpali.py:106 and main.py:288-290; it is not folded into this repair and is not decided here."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/src/backend/colpali.py::SimMapGenerator._prepare_similarity_map_tensor", "what_it_does": "Builds a zero float32 tensor of shape (maps, query tokens, n_patch, n_patch) and fills it with each Vespa summary cell's value at its query token and patch position, skipping patches at or beyond the image sequence length.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [126, 160], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "The loop at lines 142-159 performs one torch element assignment per Vespa cell, each with torch dispatch overhead, and the cell count scales with documents times query tokens times patches. Edit: inside the existing loop, store each value in a dict keyed by (idx, query_token, patch // n_patch, patch % n_patch) so later duplicates overwrite earlier ones as today, hoist the image_seq_length lookup out of the loop, then after the loop write all entries with one index_put_ over a float32 value tensor. The mechanism is removing per-cell torch dispatch in favour of one batched kernel; the output tensor, dtype and last-wins values are unchanged. Sole-caller evidence: _prepare_similarity_map_tensor is called only at colpali.py:91; out-of-range rows still raise IndexError, the same exception type."}]}
