{"step": 2, "unit": "feed_to_vespa.py::update_endpoint", "what_it_does": "Reads indexed docids, optionally deletes all of them, computes the feed docid set, deletes indexed docs missing from the feed and feeds each file through the vespa CLI, printing progress.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [152, 158, 172, 177], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "With do_index_removal_before_feed, line 177 DELETEs ids already DELETEd on line 158 with no PUT in between. Repair: guard line 177 with if not do_remove_index and keep the prints. The remote state is unchanged, and vespa_delete raises on connection failure before the second loop. Shipped configs set the flag to false, so the saving only applies when removal is enabled."}, {"label": "b", "lines": [153], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Line 154 prints the count of docids_in_index unconditionally, so skipping the visit changes stdout."}, {"label": "c", "lines": [164, 166], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "The shipped configs list several feed_endpoints sharing vespaapps_index.json, so get_feed_docids re-reads and re-parses the same files per endpoint. Repair: an optional feed_cache dict passed from main and used on a miss only. A failed read stores nothing, so the exception path is unchanged. update_endpoint has one caller, main line 201."}, {"label": "d", "lines": [166], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "docids_in_feed = docids_in_feed.union(...) copies the accumulated set per index file. Repair: docids_in_feed.update(...); the set is local and used only for len and difference. An unknown doc type raises TypeError either way, with the same message."}, {"label": "e", "lines": [175, 176], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "The per-document To Remove print is stdout the workflow logs, so changing or merging it changes printed output."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "feed_to_vespa.py::vespa_remove", "what_it_does": "Issues one HTTP DELETE per document id through vespa_delete and discards every response.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [64, 68], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "The parse is in vespa_delete (session.delete(url).json()), outside this unit. Dropping .json() stops a non-JSON error body from raising JSONDecodeError, which changes the exception type. Batching needs a different transport."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "incremental-search/search-as-you-type/feed_to_vespa.py::vespa_post", "what_it_does": "Sends one document to the Vespa document API by spawning a curl subprocess and returns curl's stdout bytes.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [48, 58], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Replacing curl with requests changes the error path: call() ignores curl's exit code and lets curl's stderr through, so a connection failure is silent today, while requests would raise. Not identical outcomes."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "incremental-search/search-as-you-type/feed_to_vespa.py::vespa_feed", "what_it_does": "Reads a feed JSON file, POSTs each document with vespa_post and prints each response body.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [83, 86], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Batching changes the per-document printed output (line 86), which the contract forbids, and the transport change has the same error-path problem as vespa_post."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "incremental-search/search-as-you-type/feed_to_vespa.py::vespa_remove", "what_it_does": "Prints a Removing line and issues one curl DELETE subprocess per document id.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [75, 80], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Replacing the curl DELETE with requests changes the error path (curl exit code is ignored today), so outcomes are not identical."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "incremental-search/search-as-you-type/feed_to_vespa.py::update_endpoint", "what_it_does": "Reads indexed docids via a visit, optionally deletes them, deletes indexed docs missing from the feed, then feeds each index file through vespa_feed while printing progress.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [139, 142, 155, 161], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Skipping the second vespa_remove changes printed output (vespa_remove prints Removing per id) and, because vespa_delete ignores curl's exit code, a transiently failed first DELETE is only retried by the second one. Remote state can change."}, {"label": "b", "lines": [149], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "The second parse is in vespa_feed (for doc in get_docs), not in this function. Removing it needs changes to vespa_feed and get_feed_docids, which are other units."}, {"label": "c", "lines": [149, 166], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "docids_in_feed = docids_in_feed.union(...) copies the accumulated set per index file. Repair: docids_in_feed.update(...); the set is fresh and local, used only for len and difference, and get_feed_docids always returns a set here."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "text-search/python/collect_training_data.py::build_dataset", "what_it_does": "Loads processed query ids, then for each unprocessed query requests features and top hits from Vespa, appends annotated rows to the training CSV and appends each query id to the processed-queries file.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [98, 99], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "The processed-queries append runs for every query, including already-processed ones, so each rerun adds duplicate lines. Repair: move the with-open-append block under the if on line 75. The printed denominator is unchanged for a given starting file; only duplicate lines stop being written. The file is read only by load_processed_queries in this module."}, {"label": "b", "lines": [75], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "Membership on a list is O(P) per query. Repair: build a set after line 72 and test against it, keeping the list so len on line 72 is unchanged; int conversion errors are raised at the same point."}, {"label": "c", "lines": [92, 97], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "The rows are written before the same query is recorded as processed. Batching the writes would let a crash record queries as processed with no rows on disk, so the on-disk state after an exception changes."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "text-search/python/collect_training_data.py::get_features", "what_it_does": "POSTs a search body to the Vespa search URL and returns the root children of the JSON response, or an empty dict after printing a message on a non-200 status.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [38], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "requests.post builds a new Session per call, so each of the two POSTs per query opens its own connection. Repair: a module-level requests.Session and session.post at line 38. Same return value and printed message; only the response cookies persist across calls, which nothing reads."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "text-search/python/convert-to-vespa-format.py::main", "what_it_does": "Reads each document's line from docs.tsv at the offset given in test-docs-offset.tsv, keeps lines whose id and field count match, and writes JSON lines to documents.jsonl in offset-file order.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [43, 45], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Sorting offsets would make reads sequential but reorders documents.jsonl, changing its content; keeping order needs holding all documents in memory."}, {"label": "b", "lines": [62], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "json.dump uses the Python-level iterencode and calls write once per fragment; out.write(json.dumps(doc)) uses the C encoder and one write per document. Same text with default arguments, and all values are strings so no exception can occur partway."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "text-search/python/extract-msmarco.py::extract_documents", "what_it_does": "Writes every document in the lookup table to docs.tsv via getcontent and writes each docid with its byte offset to docs-offset.tsv.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [84, 86], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Writing fewer documents changes both output files, and sample-queries-and-documents.py select_documents samples from every key of docs-offset.tsv, so its output would change too."}, {"label": "b", "lines": [85], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "out.tell() on a text-mode file flushes the buffer and seeks once per document, about 3.2M times on the full corpus. Repair: track a running byte count from len(s.encode('utf8')) per document; the file is written in utf-8 with mode w, so the offsets are identical on Linux (newline translation aside)."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "text-search/python/extract-msmarco.py::load_msmarco_queries", "what_it_does": "Reads the doctrain queries file and returns query id to normalised text; the qrel argument is passed in but unused.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [20, 27], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Skipping ids not in qrel saves work only if some queries lack judgements, which is not shown in the repo; the queries and qrels come from the same split."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "text-search/python/sample-queries-and-documents.py::load_queries", "what_it_does": "Reads the queries TSV, normalises each query with a regex substitution and lower-casing, and returns a dict of query text and relevant doc ids.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [29], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Not output-identical: re.sub followed by lower() can produce a combining mark that the word class does not match, so the second pass changes some queries (for example U+0130)."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "text-video-search/src/python/app.py::get_predefined_queries", "what_it_does": "Fetches the remote predefined_queries.txt on each call and returns its non-empty lines for st.selectbox when the checkbox is on.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [33, 36], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "@st.cache on the TextProcessor-style decorator (line 23) would return the first fetched list for the life of the process, so later changes to the remote file would not be seen. The repo gives no evidence the file is static."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "text-video-search/src/python/embedding.py::compute_and_send_video_embeddings", "what_it_does": "For each CLIP model in turn, builds a VideoFeedDataset and DataLoader over the videos and sends each batch of per-frame documents to Vespa, printing progress.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [145, 164], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Decoding once per video needs a video-outer loop, which changes the order of printed progress and of the Vespa batches, or keeping all decoded frames in memory across models. The notebook calling this function would see changed output too."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "text-video-search/src/python/embedding.py::VideoFeedDataset.__getitem__", "what_it_does": "Decodes a video's frames, converts each to PIL, encodes each frame with the CLIP image encoder one at a time and returns the per-frame Vespa documents.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [98, 99], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Batching the frames would cut per-call overhead, but a batched forward is not guaranteed bit-identical to batch size 1 in float32, and the returned values are sent to Vespa, so the low-order digits could change."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "text-video-search/src/python/embedding.py::extract_images", "what_it_does": "Decodes every frame of a video at 1 fps into a list and returns the sample_images selection of number_frames equally spaced frames.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [39, 52], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "For number_frames 0 the current path returns an array of shape (0, H, W, 3) with dtype uint8, while an index-first version returns float64 of shape (0,). The return value changes on that input. Decoding, the costly part, still runs over every frame."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "text-video-search/src/python/embedding.py::send_video_embeddings", "what_it_does": "Posts a batch of document updates to Vespa, prints the response summary and raises ValueError if any update failed, retried up to three times by tenacity.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [114, 128], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "A targeted retry of failed documents changes the printed Successfully sent count and failure list, which the contract forbids."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "news/src/python/convert_embeddings_to_vespa_format.py::convert_user_embeddings", "what_it_does": "Reads the user embeddings TSV into numpy float32 vectors and writes a Vespa feed JSON array with one put per user, each embedding formatted to six decimals.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [39], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "Iterating a numpy array makes one numpy scalar per element; joining over embedding.tolist() gives the same float values in one conversion. '%f' of a float32 converts to the same Python float, so the bytes are identical."}]}
