{"step": 2, "unit": "news/src/python/create_bert_embeddings.py::create_embeddings", "what_it_does": "For each unique docid, tokenizes title and abstract, runs one BertModel forward at batch size 1 and writes the first-token 512-float vector as a line, printing progress.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [51, 59], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "Each forward builds an autograd graph and keeps saved activations. Repair: import torch and wrap the model call in torch.no_grad(); forward values are identical, and no graph nodes are allocated per document."}, {"label": "b", "lines": [59], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "outputs[0].tolist()[0][0] converts the full 1 x seq_len x 512 output to Python floats to keep 512 of them. outputs[0][0][0].tolist() yields the same 512 floats, so write_embedding receives an equal list."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "news/src/python/create_bert_embeddings.py::write_embedding", "what_it_does": "Writes a tab followed by the embedding values, each formatted with %.4f and comma-joined, to an open file handle.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [68, 73], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "The loop issues about 1000 f.write calls per document. Repair: one f.write of the tab plus the comma-joined '%.4f' strings. The bytes are identical, including the empty case, and the only caller is create_embeddings line 59."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "news/src/python/create_category_ctrs.py::write_news_category_ctr_update", "what_it_does": "Streams a JSON array to news_category_ctr_update.json with one Vespa update per news id, each assigning the global CTR reference and a one-cell category_tensor.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [76], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "The category_tensor string depends only on category, so a dict from category to formatted string, filled on a miss, gives the same bytes with one format per category instead of per item. Impact is low next to the file writes."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "news/src/python/evaluate.py::calc_impression", "what_it_does": "For one impression, fetches the user's embedding from Vespa, queries candidate news with it and returns the candidate predictions and the labels.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [72, 73], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "A module-level dict from user_id to the user vector, filled on a miss, skips a Vespa round trip for repeated user ids. A failed lookup is not cached, so the exception re-raises at the same impression. calc_impression has one caller, evaluate.py line 88."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "news/src/python/evaluate.py::calc_metrics", "what_it_does": "Reads the full impressions file, draws sample_size impressions with random.sample, scores each via Vespa and returns auc, mrr and ndcg.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [86], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Sampling before parsing keeps the random draws, but the repair stops validating unsampled rows, so a malformed row that raises today no longer raises unless sampled."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "news/src/python/evaluate.py::read_impressions_file", "what_it_does": "Parses every row of an impressions TSV into a dict with user_id, news_ids and labels and returns the complete list.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [25, 47], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "calc_metrics needs every row in the returned list (len, enumerate, random.sample), so skipping parsing inside this function changes the return value; the only skip-parsing variant is the calc_metrics repair, which fails the exception check."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "news/src/python/evaluate.py::find_hit", "what_it_does": "Returns the first Vespa hit child whose news_id equals the given id, or None.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [55, 68], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "The cost is candidate count squared per impression, small next to the HTTP calls. A dict index needs building in predictions, outside this unit, and it changes exceptions for children without news_id."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "news/src/python/metrics.py::ndcg_score", "what_it_does": "Computes normalised DCG at cutoff k for one impression by dividing the DCG of prediction-ordered labels by the ideal DCG.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [18, 30], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "The ideal DCG is computed once per call. The repeat is across calls (k=5 and k=10 sort the same labels), and sharing that needs state outside this unit."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "news/src/python/metrics.py::mrr_score", "what_it_does": "Computes reciprocal-rank MRR for one impression from the prediction-ordered labels.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [43, 47], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "One argsort per call. The repeated sort is across dcg_score and mrr_score callers, needing cross-call state; a negated-score argsort would change tie order."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "news/src/python/metrics.py::group_auc", "what_it_does": "Computes sklearn roc_auc_score per impression, averages them and rounds to four decimals.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [8, 15], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "The roc_auc_score call is the metric itself. A hand-written AUC changes float results in the last bits, and roc_auc_score raises for single-class impressions, which a replacement must reproduce."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "news/src/python/mind_data.py::MindData.read_data", "what_it_does": "Reads one impressions TSV, parses each row's time, user, history and candidates, and appends a dict with user_index, timestamp, news_indices and labels.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [93, 101], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "The timestamp key is unread in the repo, but strptime raises ValueError on a malformed date, and removing it lets the same input load without error."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "news/src/python/mind_data.py::MindData.sample_training_data", "what_it_does": "Subsamples train impressions with prob, expands them via add_impressions and wraps the rows in a TensorDataset and a RandomSampler DataLoader for one epoch.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [144, 157], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Each call draws new random subsample and negative decisions, so the epoch data differs per call. Caching would skip those draws and change the global random state later code sees. The per-sample lookups are in add_impressions, not here."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "news/src/python/mind_data.py::MindData.add_impressions", "what_it_does": "For one train impression, pairs each clicked candidate with sampled skipped candidates and appends user, news, category, subcategory, entity and label values to shared lists.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [181, 201], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "Lines 189-191 and 198-200 subscript self.news_content[idx] three times per generated row. Repair: bind content = self.news_content[idx] once per loop body and take the three fields from it. Values, order and the KeyError on a missing index are unchanged; sole caller is sample_training_data."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "news/src/python/mind_data.py::MindData.sample_valid_data", "what_it_does": "Builds a list of per-impression tensor tuples for the evaluation loop, optionally over the train set, keeping impressions with mixed labels and subsampling with prob.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [159, 179], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "With train=True, the same tuples are rebuilt every epoch. Repair: a cache on self keyed by impression index, while still calling random.random() once per impression in the same order so the RNG stream is unchanged. Callers (train_mf.py:85, train_cold_start.py:124) only read the tuples. The cache keeps the train tensors alive for the process lifetime, a memory cost."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "news/src/python/mind_data.py::MindData.read_news", "what_it_does": "Parses each news row, collects WikidataIds from title and abstract entities, and stores category, subcategory and the first two entity indices per news id.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [63, 74], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Dropping the second entity column is not pure: lookup_entity_index on that id registers it in entity_map, which changes num_entities (the nn.Embedding size) and later entity indices."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "news/src/python/train_cold_start.py::eval_model", "what_it_does": "Runs the content-based model on each impression from sample_valid_data under no_grad, collects predictions and labels and prints group AUC, MRR, NDCG@5 and NDCG@10.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [130, 135], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Batching or precomputing news embeddings changes the shapes of the Linear layers and the sum reduction, so the float outputs cannot be shown bit-identical, and the printed metrics are rounded to 4 places."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "news/src/python/train_cold_start.py::save_embeddings", "what_it_does": "Computes the full user and news embedding tables from the model and writes them to data_dir as TSV files.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [146, 160], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "The recomputation and writes are the function's whole job; the waste is in the caller deciding to call it every epoch. No edit inside this body removes it. Handled by train_model label a."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "news/src/python/train_cold_start.py::write_embeddings", "what_it_does": "Writes one line per id: the id, a tab, then the row values formatted with %.6f and comma-joined.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [146, 160], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "embeddings[index].tolist() is a per-row tensor view and conversion. Repair: rows = embeddings.tolist() once before the loop and rows[index] inside. The float values and the %.6f join are unchanged, and a bad index still raises IndexError. The only caller is save_embeddings. Peak memory rises because all rows are converted up front."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "news/src/python/train_cold_start.py::train_epoch", "what_it_does": "Runs one epoch of minibatch training with BCE loss, accumulates batch loss tensors into total_loss and prints the total and average.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [99], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "The printed line formats total_loss as a tensor, so the grad_fn repr is part of the output; changing its type changes printed text. The retained graph is negligible."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "news/src/python/train_cold_start.py::train_model", "what_it_does": "Runs the content-based training loop; after every epoch prints train and validation metrics via eval_model and rewrites the two embedding files through save_embeddings.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [116, 120], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "Only the embedding rewrite is guarded: if epoch == epochs - 1, so save_embeddings runs once after the last epoch. The evals stay, since they print and consume the global RNG. The final files are byte-identical and epochs=0 still writes nothing. Caveat: a run killed before its last epoch leaves no intermediate snapshot."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "news/src/python/train_mf.py::eval_model", "what_it_does": "Runs the MF model on each impression under no_grad, collects predictions and labels and prints group AUC, MRR, NDCG@5 and NDCG@10.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [91, 95], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Batching changes the shapes of the elementwise multiply and the sum, so last-bit float changes can flip a printed 4-place digit. Not verified by a run, and it holds all impressions in memory."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "news/src/python/train_mf.py::main", "what_it_does": "Seeds the RNGs, loads MIND data, trains the MF model, evaluates the final model on train and valid, prints both metric dicts and saves the embedding TSVs.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [145, 146], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "When the last epoch already ran the 10-epoch evaluation, the two stored metric dicts can be printed instead of re-running eval_model on identical weights, saving one full train-set pass and one valid pass. Printed lines identical. train_model and eval_model have no other importer; no random draws follow these calls."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "news/src/python/train_mf.py::train_model", "what_it_does": "Runs the MF training loop with fresh negative samples each epoch and every tenth epoch prints train and validation metric dicts.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [79, 81], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "The train-set dict is printed, and sample_valid_data draws random.random() per impression, which advances the global stream used by the next epoch's training data. Removing or moving the call changes the trained weights."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "news/src/python/vespa_client.py::query_news", "what_it_does": "Posts a nearest-neighbour news search with the user vector, candidate filter and timeout to Vespa and returns the parsed JSON.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [52, 67], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "requests.post opens a new connection per call; repair: a module-level requests.Session used for the post, keeping the same data body, timeout field and exception types. Callers are evaluate.py line 53 and user_search.py line 18, which read only the JSON. The module-level session must be created by this repair itself, not borrowed from another unit's repair."}]}
