{"step": 2, "unit": "rag-blueprint/eval/train_lightgbm.py::perform_cross_validation", "what_it_does": "Stratified k-fold LightGBM training on the CSV features with categorical encoding and feature renaming, logs CV metrics, then trains and writes a final model with original feature names restored.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [181, 191], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Removing lgb_train from valid_sets removes the train metric from the log_evaluation output printed every 100 rounds, which changes printed output; early stopping inputs also change."}, {"label": "b", "lines": [151, 163], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "One Dataset with subset per fold keeps the parent's bin boundaries, while the per-fold Dataset bins on the fold's training rows. Histograms, trees and metrics change, so it is not identical."}, {"label": "c", "lines": [265, 275], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Sequential re.sub over the whole string can rename a name that a later entry also matches, and it rewrites dictionary keys such as feature_infos. A single dict walk does not give identical output on every input."}]}
