{"step": 2, "unit": "test/pseudo_terminal.py::Log.flush", "what_it_does": "The flush method of the file-like Log object that pexpect calls after each write of a read chunk, flushing sys.stdout so output appears as it arrives.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [35, 36], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "pexpect calls flush on every chunk, so the method must stay. An empty body changes when stdout bytes are emitted and how they interleave with stderr ERROR lines, which is observable output timing."}]}
