{"step": 2, "unit": "test/test.py::run_url", "what_it_does": "Prints a header, fetches each comma-separated entry (urlopen for http, file read otherwise), concatenates the bytes in order and passes them to process_page.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [304, 315], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Keep-alive via http.client changes exception types that run_config depends on (HTTPError vs RuntimeError). De-duplication changes the concatenated bytes within one comma list, and a cross-call cache would return stale content. The configured entries are local paths, so the urlopen path is not exercised anyway."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/prepare_feed_deploy.py::download_pdf", "what_it_does": "Downloads one PDF with up to max_attempts tries, derives a safe filename, writes it under pdfs/ and returns the path or None.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [265, 268], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "When the safe filename is '_', continue runs before attempt += 1 and the loop re-GETs the same URL forever with no sleep. Repair: increment attempt before continue so the branch counts toward max_attempts and the function returns None. That branch never wrote or returned before, so every terminating input is unchanged. The original does not terminate on this input, so the harness may report it as blocked."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/prepare_feed_deploy.py::float_to_binary_embedding", "what_it_does": "Converts a dict of float embedding rows into a dict of int8 lists holding the sign bits packed eight per byte, one list per key.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [584, 592], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "About four numpy calls per row per page become a few whole-array calls: stack the rows, compare with 0, packbits along axis 1, astype int8, then row.tolist() per key. Keep the original loop as fallback for empty or ragged input. packbits on axis 1 equals per-row packbits, and the last-byte padding matches. Only caller is line 611."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/prepare_feed_deploy.py::generate_embeddings", "what_it_does": "Runs the ColPali model over the page images through a DataLoader and returns one numpy array of per-page patch embeddings, with batch_size meant to group images.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [555, 559], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "The DataLoader is built without batch_size, so the batch_size=2 parameter is ignored and the model runs once per page. Repair: pass batch_size=batch_size. The collate function uses padding to a fixed length, so batch composition does not change sequence length. Batched matmuls may change float rounding in the last bits, and the iteration count changes."}, {"label": "b", "lines": [561, 568], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "The premise is wrong: np.concatenate converts each view with one bulk copy, so the same bytes are copied either way. Removing the per-image view saves microseconds against a full model forward."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/prepare_feed_deploy.py::generate_queries", "what_it_does": "Sends one page image and the query prompt to Gemini and returns the parsed JSON dict of queries, or six empty strings on any error.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [457, 459], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Reusing saved queries needs a reader of output/pdf_pages.json, which has none (the reader is commented out). Reusing stale output replaces fresh LLM output, and the empty fallback would be cached as valid. Concurrency changes the function to async and breaks its caller."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/refeed_from_hf.py::pil_to_base64", "what_it_does": "Encodes a PIL image to JPEG at default quality and returns the base64 text.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [24, 30], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "The input is already decoded here, so the stored bytes are not available. Returning base64 of the original bytes changes the return value for every caller. Avoiding the decode needs a change at the module-level load_dataset cast and in process_item_for_vespa."}]}
