{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/src/backend/colpali.py::SimMapGenerator.should_filter_token", "what_it_does": "Returns True when a query token matches a fixed set of filter patterns (special tokens, whitespace, punctuation, leading underscore, the word Question, a lone sentencepiece space).", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [253], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "re.compile on a constant is served from re's internal cache, so the removable work is the per-call cache lookup. Repair: a precompiled pattern, returning the same bool for both callers. Saving is small (about 100 calls per query), so it is likely to measure as negligible."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/src/backend/colpali.py::SimMapGenerator.gen_similarity_maps", "what_it_does": "Loads each input image as RGB with a copy and its size, computes normalised similarity maps per query token and yields each non-filtered token's blended PNG as base64.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [83, 86], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Only the size is needed downstream, but _load_image wraps decode failures as ValueError through convert('RGB'). A lazy size read would accept corrupt bodies that raise today, changing the exception contract."}, {"label": "b", "lines": [83, 88], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "processed_images is never read. Removing it saves no work, only residency of decoded pages, so there is no energy mechanism."}]}
