{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/src/backend/vespa_app.py::VespaQueryClient.query_vespa_bm25", "what_it_does": "Sends the query text, an optional qt tensor and the bm25 or bm25_sim ranking to Vespa and returns the JSON response.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [129, 153], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "pyvespa creates a new AsyncClient per context entry (VespaAsync __aenter__/__aexit__), and a shared client needs an owner outside this unit; this method also runs on a separate event loop via asyncio.run in the sim-map path."}, {"label": "b", "lines": [129, 153], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "The bm25 profile in pdf_page.sd reads query(qt) only inside the function used by bm25_sim. Repair: include input.query(qt) only when sim_map is true. Non-sim BM25 calls stop converting and serialising the token-by-128 tensor. Sim queries still send it. Not verified against a running Vespa."}]}
