{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/src/main.py::full_image", "what_it_does": "Returns an HTML img with the full JPEG of a document as a data URI, fetching from Vespa and writing to disk on a miss, or base64-encoding the disk copy on a hit.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [322, 341], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "On a disk hit every request reopens the JPEG and base64-encodes it. Repair: an lru_cache-backed helper keyed by path returning the same base64 string; the miss branch is unchanged. Route called only from app.py line 638; the readers of the files do not use this cache. maxsize bounds memory."}, {"label": "b", "lines": [322, 341], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Batching is set by the frontend issuing one request per result (app.py line 638), outside this unit. Coalescing concurrent misses would skip the debug log line for the waiting request and change the number of Vespa queries."}]}
