{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/src/main.py::message_generator", "what_it_does": "Streams Gemini's answer over server-sent events, after waiting up to 10 seconds for the full images, converting newlines to br tags in the accumulated text.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [364, 382], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Image.open is lazy and reads only headers, and the wait loop stops once enough images exist, so the reopen work is a few header reads per tick. Keeping handles open across ticks changes what is read when the file is still being written."}, {"label": "b", "lines": [403], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "The replace reruns over the whole accumulated text on every chunk, which is quadratic in the reply length. Repair: replace in chunk.text only and append the converted piece. A single-newline pattern gives the same string, and the replacement contains no newline, so no new matches."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "visual-retrieval-colpali/tests/huggingface_smoke.py::main", "what_it_does": "Imports the Space app with a test client, checks three routes return 200 and, with --load-model, asserts the LoRA-B weights are non-zero and the query embeddings are finite 2-D with width 128.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [66, 70], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "The LoRA-B checks build autograd graph nodes for each parameter, since loaded parameters require grad. Repair: wrap the check in torch.no_grad() or use detach. Assertion results and messages are unchanged; the model is local to main. The saving is small."}]}
