{"step": 2, "unit": "examples/ecommerce-user-preferences/webapp/app.py::chat", "what_it_does": "Builds the OpenAI request from the system prompt, facet context and session history, calls the model, stores preferences and queries Vespa for results and facets.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [435], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "load_system_prompt is called only here, before the try block. Hoisting it to import time makes app.py fail at import on an unreadable file and stops picking up edits to system_prompt.txt while the server runs. Saving is one small file read per chat request, negligible next to the LLM call."}, {"label": "b", "lines": [445], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "The suspected waste is the print of the system prompt, and removing it changes printed output, which the contract forbids."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "examples/ecommerce-user-preferences/webapp/app.py::get_car_image", "what_it_does": "Returns a cached image URL for a make and model, otherwise fetches one from Wikipedia and caches it, returning 404 when none is found.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [571, 577], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Caching the negative would write None into IMAGE_CACHE, which get_car_image (lines 563-565) would return as a 200 with null, and get_wikipedia_image (lines 200-205) would pick up as a similar-make hit. A transient timeout would become permanent until restart."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "examples/ecommerce-user-preferences/webapp/app.py::get_wikipedia_image", "what_it_does": "Searches Wikipedia for a make and model, lists page images, returns the first suitable URL, caches hits and falls back to a similar make.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [137, 152, 170, 185], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "The fallback loop (lines 167-196) re-requests imageinfo for titles the first loop already tried and got no URL for. Repair: keep a set of titles from the first loop and skip them in the second. Return values and prints unchanged; each skipped request is one Wikipedia round trip saved. Called only from get_car_image line 569."}, {"label": "b", "lines": [137, 152, 170, 185], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Batching titles into one imageinfo request needs the response pages mapped back to titles, which MediaWiki pageids and redirects make unverifiable offline. The first title succeeds on the common path, so batching would also add fetches there."}, {"label": "c", "lines": [86, 88], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "requests.get opens and closes a new session per call, so each Wikipedia request pays a new TCP and TLS setup. Repair: one requests.Session inside the function, used for every search and imageinfo call in the same invocation (lines 86 and 88 alone would save nothing). Same headers, params, timeouts and exceptions."}, {"label": "d", "lines": [207, 214], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Same readers as get_car_image label a: caching None blocks the similar-make fallback (lines 200-205) and makes a transient timeout permanent."}]}
