{"step": 2, "unit": "text-search/python/convert-to-vespa-format.py::main", "what_it_does": "Reads each document's line from docs.tsv at the offset given in test-docs-offset.tsv, keeps lines whose id and field count match, and writes JSON lines to documents.jsonl in offset-file order.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [43, 45], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Sorting offsets would make reads sequential but reorders documents.jsonl, changing its content; keeping order needs holding all documents in memory."}, {"label": "b", "lines": [62], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "json.dump uses the Python-level iterencode and calls write once per fragment; out.write(json.dumps(doc)) uses the C encoder and one write per document. Same text with default arguments, and all values are strings so no exception can occur partway."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "text-search/python/extract-msmarco.py::extract_documents", "what_it_does": "Writes every document in the lookup table to docs.tsv via getcontent and writes each docid with its byte offset to docs-offset.tsv.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [84, 86], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Writing fewer documents changes both output files, and sample-queries-and-documents.py select_documents samples from every key of docs-offset.tsv, so its output would change too."}, {"label": "b", "lines": [85], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "out.tell() on a text-mode file flushes the buffer and seeks once per document, about 3.2M times on the full corpus. Repair: track a running byte count from len(s.encode('utf8')) per document; the file is written in utf-8 with mode w, so the offsets are identical on Linux (newline translation aside)."}]}
