{"step": 2, "unit": "news/src/python/create_bert_embeddings.py::create_embeddings", "what_it_does": "For each unique docid, tokenizes title and abstract, runs one BertModel forward at batch size 1 and writes the first-token 512-float vector as a line, printing progress.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [51, 59], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "Each forward builds an autograd graph and keeps saved activations. Repair: import torch and wrap the model call in torch.no_grad(); forward values are identical, and no graph nodes are allocated per document."}, {"label": "b", "lines": [59], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "outputs[0].tolist()[0][0] converts the full 1 x seq_len x 512 output to Python floats to keep 512 of them. outputs[0][0][0].tolist() yields the same 512 floats, so write_embedding receives an equal list."}]}
