{"step": 2, "unit": "news/src/python/mind_data.py::MindData.sample_training_data", "what_it_does": "Subsamples train impressions with prob, expands them via add_impressions and wraps the rows in a TensorDataset and a RandomSampler DataLoader for one epoch.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [144, 157], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "Each call draws new random subsample and negative decisions, so the epoch data differs per call. Caching would skip those draws and change the global random state later code sees. The per-sample lookups are in add_impressions, not here."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "news/src/python/mind_data.py::MindData.add_impressions", "what_it_does": "For one train impression, pairs each clicked candidate with sampled skipped candidates and appends user, news, category, subcategory, entity and label values to shared lists.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [181, 201], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "Lines 189-191 and 198-200 subscript self.news_content[idx] three times per generated row. Repair: bind content = self.news_content[idx] once per loop body and take the three fields from it. Values, order and the KeyError on a missing index are unchanged; sole caller is sample_training_data."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "news/src/python/mind_data.py::MindData.sample_valid_data", "what_it_does": "Builds a list of per-impression tensor tuples for the evaluation loop, optionally over the train set, keeping impressions with mixed labels and subsampling with prob.", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [159, 179], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "With train=True, the same tuples are rebuilt every epoch. Repair: a cache on self keyed by impression index, while still calling random.random() once per impression in the same order so the RNG stream is unchanged. Callers (train_mf.py:85, train_cold_start.py:124) only read the tuples. The cache keeps the train tensors alive for the process lifetime, a memory cost."}]}
